Package: gridforge
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         qt6-qpa-plugins,
         qt6-svg-plugins
Recommends: gridforge-calculix
Suggests: freecad,
          paraview
Description: meshing and simulation workbench
 GridForge takes a part's geometry (STEP, or a .brep from FreeCAD with its
 named groups), meshes it, sets up materials, loads and supports, solves
 it through an installable toolkit, and shows how it responds. Results
 leave as files for ParaView.
 .
 Every input, mesh, deck and result is kept and traced to what made it.
 This package carries GridForge's own build of the Netgen mesher, from the
 fork it is tested with.

Package: gridforge-calculix
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         gridforge (= ${binary:Version})
Description: CalculiX toolkit for the GridForge workbench
 Lets GridForge solve structural studies with CalculiX: the toolkit's
 manifest, its adapter, and CalculiX CrunchiX (ccx) 2.23, built from its
 released source, run as a separate program.
